SUMMARY:WNC Sierra Club 11/4: The Conservation Power of Art
DESCRIPTION:WNC Sierra Club\nMark your calendars for our Nov. 4 program ab
 out the conservation power of art\, featuring local artist Spencer Beals a
 nd Doc Varn of Preserving a Picturesque America.\n\n**Spencer Beals** is a
 n Asheville-based artist and community organizer. He has been making art i
 n the River Arts District full-time for the last four years despite losing
  his life’s work in Hurricane Helene. He continues to host Sketchbook Cl
 ub\, Nature Journaling Club and conservation based art and storytelling ev
 ents.\n\n**Doc Varn** will talk about his work with the nonprofit Preservi
 ng a Picturesque America (PAPA) to continue the tradition of using the pow
 er of the arts to preserve and conserve across the country. He will share 
 stories and visuals of how they find the exact locations where artists of 
 the 1800s created the art that inspired the creation of state and national
  parks across America. Once rediscovered\, regional artists create modern 
 depictions of these locations to share how things have changed\, sometimes
  in triumph and sometimes sharing our mistakes.\n\nThe WNC Sierra Club mee
 ts monthly in Room 102 at UNCA’s Reuter Center on Campus Drive and simul
 taneously on [Zoom](https://unca-edu.zoom.us/j/85189349413?pwd=QmorsXPwjbS
 0BgiLR7xLItF3M1atab.1).\n\n**Parking at UNC Asheville:** If you do not hav
 e a parking sticker from OLLI\, you'll need to register for parking either
  ahead of time at [unca.aimsparking.com](unca.aimsparking.com) or at the R
 euter Center on the night of the meeting. The latest information about fee
 s and requirements can be found at that link. There are no visitor fees af
 ter 5 p.m.
